1.1.3.4 IcingConditions
The FAA defines icing conditions in Appendix C the Federal Aviation Regulations (FAR) Part 25/29.
Icing is defined by the variables of cloud liquid water content, the mean effective diameter of the cloud
droplets, the ambient air temperature, and the interrelationship of these three parameters (28). The
conditions are separated into two categories: continuous maximum icing and intermittent maximum
icing. The primary difference between the two is that intermittent icing generally is more severe
than continuous maximum. Table 3 and Figure 7 detail these differences.


