As explained in Section 1.1.2.2, shedding of ice is an issue inherent to rotorcraft. High centrifugal
forces place significant loads on accreted ice, causing it to release from the rotor and potentially
impact the fuselage. More importantly for this research, shedding has an effect on rotor
performance and ice accretion profile.
2.3.3.1 SheddingConcept
The ARISP model of shedding is generally similar to that contained in Reference (55). Accreted ice
is subjected to many forces, with the most important shown in Figure 28.


